 ## Overview
-The Gaussian Widget is an interactive interface component that defines transfer functions in a reduced-dimensional domain (e.g., 3D) by mapping input feature vectors to colors using a Gaussian distribution centered at a user-selected location [S1]. It solves the problem of manually tuning volumetric appearance by providing a visual, direct-manipulation interface where Gaussian parameters (position and spread) map directly to transfer function properties [S1]. It differs from nearest alternatives by mapping feature vectors directly to colors via a single Gaussian distribution rather than composing piecewise segments or arbitrary shader parameters [S1].
+The Gaussian Widget is an interactive interface component that defines transfer functions in a reduced-dimensional domain (e.g., 3D) by mapping input feature vectors to colors using a Gaussian distribution centered at a user-selected location [S1]. It solves the problem of manually tuning volumetric appearance by providing a visual, direct-manipulation interface where Gaussian parameters (position and spread) map directly to transfer function properties [S1]. It differs from its sibling [Piecewise Gaussian Transfer Function Widget](7724-piecewise-gaussian-transfer-function-widget.md) by mapping feature vectors to colors via a single distribution rather than composing multiple piecewise Gaussian functions [S1].
 
